WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.039
Four routes can read the same invoice. One costs one unit,

2
00:00:04.039 --> 00:00:08.018
one costs four, one costs nine, and one asks a human.

3
00:00:08.018 --> 00:00:09.465
Which route is efficient?

4
00:00:09.965 --> 00:00:14.577
Price alone cannot answer. The route must preserve the invoice total,

5
00:00:14.577 --> 00:00:18.770
vendor, date, and privacy rule under a fixed acceptance test.

6
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.112
So begin with a task ticket, not a model menu.

7
00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:27.338
The ticket names quality, authority, risk, deadline, and the cost classes

8
00:00:27.338 --> 00:00:28.875
we promise to count.

9
00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:33.163
Now the candidate routes become comparable: a versioned parser,

10
00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:36.951
a small specialist, a frontier model, and human review.

11
00:00:36.951 --> 00:00:39.055
Each keeps its own fallback.

12
00:00:39.555 --> 00:00:44.591
Always choosing the strongest route can preserve quality while spending nine

13
00:00:44.591 --> 00:00:48.254
units on every ordinary invoice. Useful work survives,

14
00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:50.085
but reuse never compounds.

15
00:00:50.585 --> 00:00:55.503
Always choosing the cheapest route looks better until a damaged scan

16
00:00:55.503 --> 00:00:59.527
drops one tax digit. The one-unit answer creates repair,

17
00:00:59.527 --> 00:01:01.315
review, and downstream correction.

18
00:01:01.815 --> 00:01:06.576
The Efficient ASI hypothesis asks for the lowest-cost authorized route that

19
00:01:06.576 --> 00:01:10.039
can satisfy the fixed predicate, not the lowest

20
00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:11.770
price on the menu.

21
00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.715
A familiar template may enter the versioned parser.

22
00:01:15.715 --> 00:01:20.452
Its output earns acceptance only after the required checks pass and

23
00:01:20.452 --> 00:01:22.175
its assumptions remain current.

24
00:01:22.675 --> 00:01:26.990
The damaged scan fails that check. The failure stays attached to

25
00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:31.305
the task as a visible residual instead of becoming cheap success.

26
00:01:31.805 --> 00:01:35.789
Fallback then escalates the same ticket to a stronger specialist or

27
00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:39.411
a human. The failed attempt remains on the bill and

28
00:01:39.411 --> 00:01:40.860
in the learning record.

29
00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:46.900
Total contract cost includes generation, context, routing, verification, repair,

30
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:52.440
review, rollback preparation, maintenance, delayed failure, and displaced work.

31
00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.999
Now predict. If the cheap route costs one, repair costs eight,

32
00:01:56.999 --> 00:02:00.319
and review costs three, is it more efficient than

33
00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.795
a verified nine-unit route?

34
00:02:02.295 --> 00:02:07.044
No. Twelve is greater than nine, and the hidden-cost win disappears.

35
00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:10.498
Efficiency belongs to the complete causal route, not

36
00:02:10.498 --> 00:02:12.225
its cheapest visible meter.

37
00:02:12.725 --> 00:02:17.609
Repeated verified work can become a parser, cache, tool, memory, proof,

38
00:02:17.609 --> 00:02:21.604
or specialist. But the artifact carries a version, assumptions,

39
00:02:21.604 --> 00:02:23.380
tests, and renewal cost.

40
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.167
When the invoice format changes, the cached route expires.

41
00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:32.930
Revalidation is not overhead added afterward; it prevents yesterday's saving

42
00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.835
from becoming tomorrow's debt.

43
00:02:35.335 --> 00:02:41.009
The routed resource can be model capacity, context, search, numerical precision,

44
00:02:41.009 --> 00:02:45.652
tools, or verification. Minimum viable intelligence is a candidate

45
00:02:45.652 --> 00:02:47.715
policy, not an axiom.

46
00:02:48.215 --> 00:02:53.096
For novel, uncertain, or high-consequence work, the strongest route plus broad

47
00:02:53.096 --> 00:02:57.976
verification may dominate. The architecture must be allowed to learn that

48
00:02:57.976 --> 00:03:00.195
selectivity has no value there.

49
00:03:00.695 --> 00:03:06.020
Scaling forecasts still matter, but a smooth loss curve is not

50
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:10.861
a capability guarantee. Preserve forecast residuals and watch operational thresholds

51
00:03:10.861 --> 00:03:14.250
without declaring every jump real or illusory.

52
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:19.524
A fair test freezes natural tasks, then compares always-cheapest, always-maximal,

53
00:03:19.524 --> 00:03:23.820
adaptive routing, and a strong monolith with tools under

54
00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.730
matched access and tuning.

55
00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:32.008
Score useful accepted work against total contract cost. Count unsafe effects,

56
00:03:32.008 --> 00:03:35.684
false refusals, recovery, latency, human burden, tail

57
00:03:35.684 --> 00:03:37.785
failures, and maintenance together.

58
00:03:38.285 --> 00:03:43.311
This chapter does not contain that result. Its support remains an

59
00:03:43.311 --> 00:03:47.880
argument; finite route fixtures organize accounting but prove no measured

60
00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.165
efficiency, transfer, safety, or ASI.

61
00:03:50.665 --> 00:03:56.069
Return to the invoice. Efficiency means the saving remains visible after

62
00:03:56.069 --> 00:04:00.490
quality, authority, verification, fallback, and repair are paid. Next,

63
00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:04.420
System Boundaries and Authority defines where permission stops.
